{
  "summary": "Converts DescriptorScriptPubKeyMan's internal mutex from a public RecursiveMutex to a private non-recursive Mutex renamed to m_desc_mutex. External callers across the wallet, RPC, and fuzzing harnesses are migrated to self-locking public member functions, while internal recursive routines are separated into lock-held helper methods. Address-availability notifications are deferred until after the mutex is released so that synchronous callbacks can safely query wallet state.",
  "problem": "DescriptorScriptPubKeyMan relied on a public RecursiveMutex, obscuring lock hierarchies, bypassing compile-time thread-safety analysis, and permitting recursive call paths. Additionally, dispatching availability change signals while holding the mutex risked re-entrancy deadlocks if synchronous listeners (such as the GUI) queried the descriptor manager during the callback.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Part of https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/19303'",
    "Commit 30c44a175e: 'Compare availability before and after each operation under the mutex, then notify after unlocking so synchronous callbacks can query the wallet safely. Notify only for a net change, including partial updates that throw, and rethrow captured exceptions after notification.'"
  ],
